   <notesStmt>
    <note type="project" target="#dat1">Whitman probably created this manuscript not long before the dedication of the Washington Monument on February 21, 1885.</note>
    <note type="work_relations" target="xxx.00343" cert="high">These early draft lines contributed to the poem published as "Ah, Not This Granite Dead and Cold" in the <hi rend="italic">Philadelphia Press</hi> on February 22, 1885. Whitman later made minor revisions and republished the poem under the title "Washington's Monument, February, 1885" in <hi rend="italic">November Boughs</hi> (1888) and in the "Sands at Seventy" annex to <hi rend="italic">Leaves of Grass</hi> (1891&#8211;1892).</note>
    
